    "notes": "Actually inspected all 25 final grade images, five cameras across master and all four levels. Public Bavarian DGM1 bare-earth samples support a 7.2 m upper/lower court difference, represented as native Y8.2/Y1. The corrected gateway and connecting wing are lower, embedded foundations extend to Y-7, and both 40-tread flights remain visible at their corrected cameras. Three contact probes have approximately 0.015 m fixture clearance and less than 0.03 m floor error in every level. Terrain is masked only beneath the closed court union; no green interpolation patches protrude through its paving. Every level unload leaves zero live geometry and restores terrain. The fixture uses 3 m samples of a 1 m product, heights rounded to 0.1 m, and a 960.7 m DHHN2016 local datum solely for verification. Samples under buildings are interpolated ground, not floor surveys. Architectural roof heights and edge foundations remain photo-fitted. Coarse Mapzen terrain was rejected as insufficient local ridge evidence. Production uses an explicit lower-court terrain reference and imposes no absolute elevation."
